# The gallery: what the engine can do, side by side on one board, behind the
# main menu. Seven worlds in rock frames, every one a pack of its own, all
# compiled together as one rule set (every name is global, so none collide):
#
#   x 1..192,    y 1..214     the 5-state busy beaver drawn as its history (packs/turing)
#   x 194..291,  y 1..64      Gosper's glider gun and an eater (packs/life)
#   x 293..382,  y 1..64      a cyclic automaton of 16 colours: spirals (packs/cyclic)
#   x 194..321,  y 66..131    rule 90 from one cell, the Sierpinski triangle, redrawn as its
#                             springs pick again (packs/elementary)
#   x 323..382,  y 66..131    Langton's ant and an LLRR ant (packs/turmite)
#   x 194..311,  y 133..214   a grove of L-system trees that wither and grow again (packs/lsystem)
#   x 313..382,  y 133..214   a fox and a flock round a pond (the built-in kinds)
#
#   make run ARGS="play saves/gallery --scenario scenarios/gallery.scenario"
#
# The boards that start full are shares in a region (`start K N / D in ...`);
# the gun and the pen are drawn. The `run` and `expect` lines at the end check
# that the worlds run side by side as each does alone.
rules ../rules ../packs/life ../packs/turing ../packs/elementary ../packs/cyclic ../packs/turmite ../packs/lsystem
seed 1
outside rock
map {
  ################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################################
